The following keywords are used to define Typed Structures:

TypeDefine Define a non-streamable type. Non-streamable types can not be saved to streams or objects.

TypeDefineStreamable Define a streamable type. Streamable types can be saved as Value Types of objects, streamed to binary, written to the filesystem etc. They require a unique ID.

TypeDefineInterface Define an interface. Typed Structure Interfaces are very similar to Java interfaces.

TypeDefinePackage Define a Typed Structure Package. A package is a non-streamable type containing functions and a ContractMembers() block only. It is a convenient way to package member functions and import them by various types.

Members Declare the typed data members of a Typed Structure.

Implements Declare that a Typed Structure implements an interface or set of interfaces.

ImportPackages Declare that a Typed Structure imports a package or set of packages.

Extends Declare that a Typed Structure interface extends another interface or set of interfaces.

ContractMembers Declare the typed data members that can be used in a Typed Structure Package. Only allowed in packages.

See also How do I define C-like structures in Slang?

TypeDefine
1. Syntax

 TypeDefine( "Scope::Name" )
 {
   ... statics                        // varName = value; , no typing
   ... functions (Func, Lambda) ...   // only Lambdas can access statics
   Members( [ BaseType ] )            // Optional Base Type for inheritance
   [ Implements( Interface, ... ) ]   // Optionally Implement an interface
   [ ImportPackages( Package, ... ) ] // Optionally Import one or more packages
   {
    ....
   };
 };
2. Example
_TYPE Test Interfaces

3. Notes
Scope and Name must be different, otherwise, secview may crash.

TypeDefineStreamable
1. Syntax

 TypeDefineStreamable( TypeID, "Scope::Name" )
 {
   ... everything the same as TypeDefine
 };
2. Example
_TYPE Test

