Referencing and Linking Non Streamable Typed Structures
To use a non streamable Typed Structure link it explicitly in the scripts that use them.

 Link("_TYPE My Type");
This is the same way that libraries are linked.
Note: The old way of defining and linking non streamable typed structures optionally suggested to add an entry in "_LIB Typed Struct Decl NS*". This used to make these type structures globally linked at the session startup time and users of these types did not have to link the _TYPE script declaring them. You may find some existing Typed Structures in these start up scripts. This is not preferred, as it slows down start-up and provides a global singleton rather than clearly defined encapsulated dependencies.

Dynamic linking of Typed Structures
In some cases the typed structure you are creating may only be known at runtime. You can instantiate a typed structure dynamically using SmartLink(). This example provides a function that provides a registry of Typed Structure name to script.


 Private::Type Instantiation = Func(
 String( Type Name ),
 Slang( Library Lookup Function ),
 Structure( Arguments ):={||},
 )
 Returns( Typed Structure() )
 {
     Lib Name = @Library Lookup Function( Type Name );
     LintPragma( "Function Called Remotely" );
     SmartLink( Lib Name );
     Return( Apply( Type Name, NamedArgs := Arguments ) );
 };
See also FAQ: When do I need to use SmartLink?

