Static Members
Define a static looking variable and lambdas that can access that variable. This static variable can only be accessed via Lambda's. Unfortunately, this variable can only be accessed via an object of that type.

 TypeDefine( "ABC::Static Member Example" ) {
   Static Member = "This is my starting state";
   Update Static Member = Lambda( Self, Update ) Returns() { Static Member = Update };
   Get Static Member   = Lambda( Self ) Returns( Any() ) Return( Static Member );
   Members() {};
 };

 TS1 = ABC::Static Member Example();
 TS2 = ABC::Static Member Example();

 Print( TS1.Get Static Member(), "\n" ); // prints "This is my starting state"
 Print( TS2.Get Static Member(), "\n" ); // prints "This is my starting state"

 TS1.Update Static Member( "Now I am updated" );

 Print( TS1.Get Static Member(), "\n" ); // prints "Now I am updated"
 Print( TS2.Get Static Member(), "\n" ); // prints "Now I am updated" ( Static member is global among all instances of TS )
